# The edges measurement turned up, all in one book. A COMMENT
# subtree hides nothing from a refresh: the dynamic block inside one
# is rewritten, and the block named inside one answers a diff, even
# though nothing there tangles. The opener and the closer fold case.
# A closer with a word after its colon still closes, and the lines
# after it are not the block's to overwrite. A book whose last line
# has no newline gains one, because saving adds it. And the two
# plan-toc blocks print different numbers for the same sites, which
# is the part-refreshed buffer: the second one is counted after the
# first has already grown.

# A book with no dynamic block in it comes through untouched. The
# newline half of that rule is pinned by TestFinalNewlineFollowsTheSave
# instead, because txtar ends every file it holds with a newline and
# cannot carry a book that lacks one.
exec babble tangle plain.org
cmp plain.org want/plain.org

exec babble tangle edges.org
cmp edges.org want/pass1.org
cmp e.go want/e.go

exec babble tangle edges.org
cmp edges.org want/pass2.org

-- edges.org --
#+title: edges
#+todo: PLANNED(p!) HOLE(h!) | LIVE(l!) DROPPED(d@)

* COMMENT A dead chapter

#+name: buried
#+begin_src go :tangle no
buried body
#+end_src

#+begin: plan-toc
#+end:

* Alive

#+name: live
#+begin_src go :tangle e.go
live body
#+end_src

A diff of a buried block against a live one:

#+BEGIN: src-block-diff :old buried :new live
#+END:

A closer with a word after the colon:

#+begin: plan-toc
#+end: ignored
this line survives
#+end:

* PLANNED A site
-- want/pass1.org --
#+title: edges
#+todo: PLANNED(p!) HOLE(h!) | LIVE(l!) DROPPED(d@)

* COMMENT A dead chapter

#+name: buried
#+begin_src go :tangle no
buried body
#+end_src

#+begin: plan-toc
- [[file:edges.org::26][26]] generated diff
- [[file:edges.org::36][36]] entry: PLANNED A site

#+end:

* Alive

#+name: live
#+begin_src go :tangle e.go
live body
#+end_src

A diff of a buried block against a live one:

#+BEGIN: src-block-diff :old buried :new live
#+begin_src diff
@@ -1 +1 @@
-buried body
+live body
#+end_src
#+END:

A closer with a word after the colon:

#+begin: plan-toc
- [[file:edges.org::26][26]] generated diff
- [[file:edges.org::44][44]] entry: PLANNED A site

#+end: ignored
this line survives
#+end:

* PLANNED A site
